{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out","id":964724,"title":"Whens next 2nd edition book coming out?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-06T19:36:41-07:00","id":964724,"title":"Whens next 2nd edition book coming out?","content":"waited over 2 years... getting kind of antsy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T19:49:19-07:00","id":964733,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Covenants is in layout. So, pretty soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T19:51:02-07:00","id":964734,"title":"","content":"You can track Secrets of the Covenants and Thousand Years of Night in every Monday Meeting Notes. There's also a Black Death chapter in the Dark Eras Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T23:10:45-07:00","id":964811,"title":"","content":"Actually, it's been almost three years, as Blood and Smoke was first published in Nov 2013, if I recall correctly. Little did you know that they would be publishing new Vampire material according to Kindred lifetimes...<br /> <br /> \u200bWith a little less snark, it's obvious that V20 (and the other 20's) are where the money is now. Just look at the book count. Still, for those of us that prefer Requiem, it's almost painful waiting for some more to consume. Could you imagine if Wizards had issued the new D&amp;D 5th edition Player's Guide and then did nothing for three years? We wouldn't get the Monsters' Manual until <b><i>August 19th, 2017.</i></b><br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not buying anything from OP until we get more Requiem material, which really pains me, as I would love to get 2nd edition Mage, and even as much as I dislike V20 now, the new Becket's (which was the first KS I haven't backed for OP.)<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd no, a chapter in Dark Eras does not count.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T06:27:04-07:00","id":964924,"title":"","content":"Do you know that you not buying it, if anything slows it down? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The more people buy it, the more gets produced. Simple as that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:12:58-07:00","id":964941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=964924#post964924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know that you not buying it, if anything slows it down? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The more people buy it, the more gets produced. Simple as that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u00b4s not THAT simple. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> If you are buying, for example, V20-stuff, you are not communicating to OPP that you want more Requiem - you\u00b4re communicating that you are interested in V20. That\u00b4s not helping Requiem getting more books, it\u00b4s only helping V20 since that is what the consumers seem to be interested in. I see where Kerensky is coming from here and I feel the same: Since my main interest in CofD lies with Requiem, I wont give my money to non-requiem products until the game I favor will get some love again. Voting with my wallet, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8497-sethnacht","name":"Sethnacht","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:38:28-07:00","id":964952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethnacht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=964941#post964941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u00b4s not THAT simple. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it doesn't seem to be that simple at all. I was asking in one of the Monday Meetings if Werewolf was getting a book, as nothing is planned, and RichT responded, 'Not every CofD line will get a book every year between GenCons, we simply don\u2019t have the space to give all 11 lines that many books. But WtF2 will be getting more Dark Eras, and most likely will get more DEs in Dark Eras 2.'<br /> <br /> I don't know what the money situation is at all, maybe World of Darkness does make more and they're trying to get as much as they can before White Wolf takes over, but it doesn't really seem like there's more World of Darkness books, the books they have coming out are leaning towards Vampire because there's only three games out, compared to Chronicle of Darkness' ten, eleven if you count 'blue book, which I do.<br /> <br /> It's frustrating, for those of us who are only really interested in some lines, to not see those lines get support. But, again, I don't know what the business side of things is like beyond what we see from the Monday Meetings, which is admittedly a lot. Some writers can to take a long time with things, because of real life concerns such as 'working to make a living,' and while Mage 20th came out, I think, really fast, Wraith 20 is still being written. Then there's the art direction, which I think only has one full-time worker and someone learning how to do it, dealing with the mercurial and limited pool of artists. It's possible that they just don't have the people to really write and organize and put out more books. There's only so many writers who have the experience and skill to be developers. It's not an easy thing at any level once you get past 'this might be a good idea for a book.'<br /> <br /> And then there's the shift in attention. Vampire doesn't seem as popular as they once were. I see a lot of more on-topic threads in the Vampire forum where someone expresses their moral distaste or disgust in what vampires are and how they don't want to play that, while other games have gotten surprising amounts of attention. And admittedly a lot of the second edition games already have books out from first edition, and a lot of the material can be transferred over, even if it isn't of the quality or with the developmental mindset of second edition. So it makes sense for something like Demon to have several books out, given its popularity, and the fact that some were promised as part of the Kickstarter. And while they may not be out yet, Vampire does have two books coming down the line, and a third planned.<br /> <br /> Even understanding that, the frustration's there. It was like during the Dark Eras voting, where you had one vote out of hundreds, and seeing the lines you like pass by Era-less. I got lucky with Werewolf on the second go around, but Vampire didn't get much beyond Regina, Hunter outside of Salem.<br /> <br /> I think I'd feel at least a little better if I knew how things were going with the whole White Wolf Publishing reincarnation. Will they ever actually do anything? Will they be taking all of World of Darkness properties? If they do, will that mean more steady flow of Chronicles of Darkness books? Or a crunch without the World of Darkness income? Will they be taking writers and artists? There is some overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-07-2016, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:06:56-07:00","id":965024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethnacht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=964941#post964941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u00b4s not THAT simple. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> If you are buying, for example, V20-stuff, you are not communicating to OPP that you want more Requiem - you\u00b4re communicating that you are interested in V20. That\u00b4s not helping Requiem getting more books, it\u00b4s only helping V20 since that is what the consumers seem to be interested in. I see where Kerensky is coming from here and I feel the same: Since my main interest in CofD lies with Requiem, I wont give my money to non-requiem products until the game I favor will get some love again. Voting with my wallet, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not talking about buying V20 stuff. Kerensky said that he will not be buying CofD books (even when he wants them like Mage), until they get more attention. Which completely baffles me. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:15:03-07:00","id":965031,"title":"","content":"Unpopular opinion: I prefer the long gaps between releases over the constant supplement treadmill of the old White Wolf days. The books we do get are far better quality, and there's not nearly so much z-splat bloat, which to be honest was pretty taxing to me during 1e. All the 1e supplements are still out there and for the most part pretty easy to adapt to 2e if you want to expand your game beyond what's in the core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965024#post965024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not talking about buying V20 stuff. Kerensky said that he will not be buying CofD books (even when he wants them like Mage), until they get more attention. Which completely baffles me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also this. I buy PDFs and hard copies of each new CofD book as it comes out (except Mummy since it's still 1e and Beast which I plan to get eventually but haven't gotten around to yet) to support the game and the company that makes it, even if I don't have an immediate use planned for the content in the book. I don't buy any cWoD material because I don't play cWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-07-2016, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:28:17-07:00","id":965043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965024#post965024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kerensky said that he will not be buying CofD books (even when he wants them like Mage), until they get more attention. Which completely baffles me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kerensky\u00b4s point was not buying anymore OP-Products until specifically Requiem (instead of CofD lines in general) gets more attention. Buying Mage 2nd edition would not increase the likelyhood of Requiem getting additional products. If you want to communicate your desire for more Requiem-products effectivly, you have to buy Requiem-Products. But since their is only one 2nd Edition-Sourcebook right now, buying a book you already own over and over again just to make its salesnumbers match those of the lines who actually get new releases is not a feasible solution, is it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8497-sethnacht","name":"Sethnacht","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:41:06-07:00","id":965055,"title":"","content":"They can take as much time as they need. 2e books have been remarkably unpolished, and it's a trend that doesn't seem to be going away. If anything it seems to be getting worse, and it's getting increasingly frustrating. If they take their time, maybe that issue will get resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:43:23-07:00","id":965058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965031#post965031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unpopular opinion: I prefer the long gaps between releases over the constant supplement treadmill of the old White Wolf days. The books we do get are far better quality, and there's not nearly so much z-splat bloat, which to be honest was pretty taxing to me during 1e. All the 1e supplements are still out there and for the most part pretty easy to adapt to 2e if you want to expand your game beyond what's in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also prefer quality over quantity, but I also want to get more Requiem-stuff. I already own all the 1st edition books as well as the 2nd edition core, so just &quot;buying what I missed in 1st edition&quot; is unfortunately not an option to fix my hunger for new and exciting Requiem-content. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8497-sethnacht","name":"Sethnacht","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:08:22-07:00","id":965086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965031#post965031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unpopular opinion: I prefer the long gaps between releases over the constant supplement treadmill of the old White Wolf days.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a way, aren't you getting the 'treadmill' of books as you are getting everything Chronicles puts out? At the least you don't seem to be having the same issue with a long gap between releases that someone who is only interested in one or two games might, no?<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone's really wanting a treadmill of stuff, but from a fans point of view there can be a reasonable desire for balance somewhere between 'monthly' and 'every three years.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:23:42-07:00","id":965105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965086#post965086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a way, aren't you getting the 'treadmill' of books as you are getting everything Chronicles puts out? At the least you don't seem to be having the same issue with a long gap between releases that someone who is only interested in one or two games might, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a sense, but they are mostly new gamelines rather than supplements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965086#post965086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone's really wanting a treadmill of stuff, but from a fans point of view there can be a reasonable desire for balance somewhere between 'monthly' and 'every three years.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, though if those are the only options I'd probably take the latter. But yeah, somewhere inbetween would be preferable. Here's hoping that when White Wolf comes out with the next edition of cWoD, it doesn't hurt OPP too much and they'll shift more focus towards CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:29:44-07:00","id":965114,"title":"","content":"The Caine and Lilith Tickets were claimed, by a husband and wife, it turns out... so it seems that Funding for OnyxPath is quite Secure...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:32:24-07:00","id":965120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965114#post965114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caine and Lilith Tickets</div> </div> </div> </div>What are these?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:39:25-07:00","id":965127,"title":"","content":"highest Tier Tickets at Grand Masquerade Coming with<ul><li>Complimentary transportation between the airport and Astor Crowne Plaza Hotel</li> <li>A suite at the Astor Crowne Plaza (September 1st - 4th)</li> <li>All registration materials will be delivered to your room at the Astor Crowne Plaza</li> <li>Admission to our exclusive VIP Party on Thursday night</li> <li>Personalized character creation and two tickets for the following events<ul><li>Blood &amp; Betrayal III <i>with 100 bonus XP on your characters</i></li> <li>Rage &amp; Retribution II <i>with 100 bonus XP on your characters</i></li> </ul></li> <li>2 tickets for the following events<ul><li>Vampires &amp; Vino</li> <li>Werewolves &amp; Whiskey</li> </ul></li> <li>Admission to The Succubus Club<ul><li>A private table for you and up to 7 guests, with champagne or vodka service</li> <li>A souvenier photograph at The Succubus Club</li> </ul></li> <li>Souvenir jewelry item</li> <li>Access to all fan community events</li> <li>Access to all open panels &amp; seminars</li> <li>A copy of The Grand Masquerade program guide</li> </ul>All for $4000<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:08:40-07:00","id":965168,"title":"","content":"OK- a couple of things. First, we are aware of how long the new VtR2 books have taken. Onyx Path works on a system of picking a developer for a game line and then letting that developer work with the writing team they prefer on each individual book. In the case of VtR2, that developer has been Rose Bailey, and because of her experience with bringing forward 2nd Editions, she has been assisting with other CofD books, including combing through the core to eliminate all the references to nWoD, as well as developing the Vtr2 books she has slated. Her Development Manager position made her part of the Onyx Path inner circle, and she was just getting the hang of that when an accident caused a debilitating shoulder injury that dropped her output to something like 10% of what she was used to accomplishing. So for this past year you can see more progress as she has been healing and getting back to her usual productivity.<br /> <br /> Including VtR2 in Dark Eras and its associated books was part of providing all of you with _something_ while she got back to speed. Understood that it's not a whole book, but it was what was possible.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Rose could not have created VtR2 without loving it, a lot, and so she has tried to keep pushing forward with the line. But even with that love for Requiem, she has identified that this current delay has been way too long, and is actively working with other folks to step in and help with the development in order to get more VtR2 books out faster in the future.<br /> <br /> Second, I'm really, really, glad to hear from folks that they want more of any given game line. That is just what a creator wants to hear! Please just bear in mind that your enjoyment of any given line, and the enjoyment you hear from folks in social media, does not change the various factors that go into getting projects approved and out the door. You love VtR2 and might be thrilled for a book a month, Bob, though, loves Mummy and wants all the Mummy we can make as fast as we can fire out the door. And Sally just wants Werewolf and nothing else! If those lines have healthy sales and we still have great ideas for them, we try and get them on our list to publish, but that list can't have infinite projects on it. Only the amount of projects that make sense for us in any given stretch of time.<br /> <br /> Which is why we have done books like Hurt Locker, or Dark Eras, or the upcoming Crossover Chronicle, so that even if we can't get out a book for a line you are into this year, we provide you with something for it that we hope will prove interesting and useful.<br /> <br /> Finally, there is some validity in the idea that a line or individual book that sells really well will increase the chance that we'll do more like it. So liking something, buying it, getting your friends to buy it, etc., all will be noticed when I look at sales numbers as one of the determining factors for what gets on the publishing list.<br /> <br /> The flip side, withholding your purchases, is more problematic. There are many reasons for lack of sales, and we have no way of knowing which of them are in play when we see a particular project lag. You are sending a message we do not have the equipment to receive and understand. For example, if Promethean 2nd has bad sales because a whole bunch of folks decide not to purchase it, even though they would like to, in order to send a message to us about publishing more VtR2 books, we are not going to understand your intent and instead will stop making Promethean 2 books because the sales indicate we will lose money trying to advance the game line.<br /> <br /> That being said, please don't buy Onyx Path projects unless you want to. Because you like the line, the individual book and what is in it, the art, the writers, Onyx Path itself; these are all great reasons to buy. Similarly, don't buy them if you don't want to, or our policies and practices, or our publishing methods, bother you. We aren't owed your money, and should expect that you will go elsewhere if what we do doesn't work for you.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:44:58-07:00","id":965195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965031#post965031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unpopular opinion: I prefer the long gaps between releases over the constant supplement treadmill of the old White Wolf days. The books we do get are far better quality, and there's not nearly so much z-splat bloat, which to be honest was pretty taxing to me during 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty of the 1E books were essentially stuff that could be made up at the game table by a reasonably competent GM, leading to z-splat bloat &quot;Les Canards are a Parisian bloodline who have perfected the duck bonding discipline known as Mallardous&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mechanically VtR2E is a very complete game, the themes are laid out clearly, there's several premade settings, alternate rules, e.t.c., so a justified supplement really has to explore some part of the world in depth in terms of lore (e.g. Secrets of the Convenets) or deal with playing, not just stats for, a character type not fully explored in the core (e.g. A Thousand Years of Night). This takes a good bit more time, but they're likely to be far better books.<br /> <br /> I'd love them a bit quicker of course, but CoD is a big line with many games!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 09-07-2016, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:01:00-07:00","id":965208,"title":"","content":"I just hope were not disappointed like we were with DotFA which had disapointments galore throughout it.. and this after being pushed back 3 or 4 times...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:19:14-07:00","id":965220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965208#post965208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope were not disappointed like we were with DotFA which had disapointments galore throughout it.. and this after being pushed back 3 or 4 times...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what the relevance is to an Exalted book not put out by Onyx Path? Different company, different processes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:57:01-07:00","id":965463,"title":"","content":"Fair enough sir.<br /> <br /> Oh Another question on Secrets of the Covenants, Think its possible some domains might have a chapter house that tolerates, or even openly, advocates, the Coil of Ziva?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T03:45:38-07:00","id":965582,"title":"","content":"I love it when we get an insight into the business side of things, for what it's worth CofD is on my to get list as is Mage when it exists it physical but more Vampire is my priority. Also I can't help but wonder if going PoD isn't hurting sales? I rarely buy stuff on line but would probably pick up any CofD book I saw in a shop, also as is you're only selling to people who set out to buy your product.<br /> I'm sure you know better but it just seems odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:26:41-07:00","id":965593,"title":"","content":"Essentially, the increase in sales would not cover the vast increase in costs involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:35:24-07:00","id":965597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965168#post965168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Bob, though, loves Mummy and wants all the Mummy we can make as fast as we can fire out the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually my name is Rob <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:58:42-07:00","id":965604,"title":"","content":"Personally, i don't mind waiting if the next product has high quality. High quality is a somewhat personal measure, yes, but is absolutely clear IMHO, that is something that has clearly increased in the last editions. I'm seriously in love with my VtR2. So... i'm expecting that level of quality, at least. (The more, the better! xD) I want more VtR2 books? Absolutely! (As more MtA2 ones pretty please!) But i'm willing to wait, and i understand the delay - thank you for the brief report on what was going on in the backstage, RichT-.<br /> <br /> That being said, the OP is right: we're thirsting for more. [In particular, that &quot;Thousand Years of Night&quot; has me salivating furiously.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:09:53-07:00","id":966050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965463#post965463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough sir.<br /> <br /> Oh Another question on Secrets of the Covenants, Think its possible some domains might have a chapter house that tolerates, or even openly, advocates, the Coil of Ziva?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually had a thought about this as well. I know normally it is harshly punished to teach a coil outside of the dragons. What if you helped someone outside the dragons learn a heretical coil to see if anything beneficial could be salvaged from it? Perhaps scales that would be valuable to the Dragons, or another coil that falls in line with the dragon way?<br /> <br /> Since it's heretical dragons are not suppose to learn it, what about a non-dragon learning it as an experiment to create a new Coil that actually falls within the dragon's philosophy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:31:48-07:00","id":966067,"title":"","content":"Just get a Twilight Judge to ok it and you're good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T00:28:53-07:00","id":966099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=966050#post966050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I actually had a thought about this as well. I know normally it is harshly punished to teach a coil outside of the dragons. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What if you helped someone outside the dragons learn a heretical coil to see if anything beneficial could be salvaged from it? Perhaps scales that would be valuable to the Dragons, or another coil that falls in line with the dragon way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not anymore. The descriptions for the Twilight Judge and Independent Study are pretty clear about saying non Dragons learn Mysteries and &quot;heretical&quot; declared acceptable for study. Nor is it a stretch to say non Dragons can discover and learn them. I would also think that Dragons would actually encourage Independent Studies to develop them as a means of skirting formal prohibitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-09-2016, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T00:44:55-07:00","id":966109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=965582#post965582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love it when we get an insight into the business side of things, for what it's worth CofD is on my to get list as is Mage when it exists it physical but more Vampire is my priority. Also I can't help but wonder if going PoD isn't hurting sales? I rarely buy stuff on line but would probably pick up any CofD book I saw in a shop, also as is you're only selling to people who set out to buy your product.<br /> I'm sure you know better but it just seems odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>For an interesting look behind that curtain at this, Caleb Stokes detailed the process of having to decide between doing Print on Demand or an offset physical print run for his own RPG on the Game Designer's Workshop series of the Roleplaying Public Radio podcast. The cost of bulk printing hardcover, full-color books of decent length and then shipping copies of those to dozens of hobby shops is enormous, and with an industry as niche as tabletop roleplaying where those books aren't guaranteed to sell... well, there's a reason the only big names left in the industry primarily fund themselves with collectible card and deluxe board games. This industry as a whole is barely profitable at the best of times, and the choice isn't really &quot;physical books in stores or print-on-demand,&quot; it's &quot;print-on-demand or we go out of business.&quot;<br /> <br /> OPP has something like four permanent employees. It just isn't feasibly for them or anyone else smaller than Wizards of the Coast to go for the old distribution model, and that's okay; things have changed in the consumer's favor with the shift to digital and PoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:37:12-07:00","id":966772,"title":"","content":"In these three years, the new gamelines (Mummy, Demon) have received much more support than vampire (about 2 or books each one, I think). And I understand perfectly, but I'm concerned. With so much new gamelines, I feel the classical gamelines receve less attention than I'd like.<br /> <br /> I think a possible solution couls be expanding the Dark Eras settings. It could be made in two ways (not incompatible):<br /> a) Including as kickstarted goals new dark eras source books. They could be new eras, or expansions of the eras of the kikstarters...<br /> b) New dark eras gamelines: requiem for Rome revised with 3 or 4 books, or Sumerian werewolves, or ancient Irem, or a series of books of a particular setting with different books for each gameline (or a book for 2 or 3 gamelines), or a dark era centered in a gameline but with a sourcebook related to the other ones...<br /> <br /> In this way, it would accomplish two goals: developing a new gameline with a full diferent setting than the other ones, and providing new material for all the others gamelines, but in a different era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:23:00-07:00","id":966812,"title":"","content":"I'd really rather have Neolithic than Sumerian for werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T12:51:46-07:00","id":966870,"title":"","content":"Yes, I'd also would love a full setting detailing the neolithic from The Sundered World. <br /> <br /> It would be an excellent way of producing a new and totally different setting than the current ones, but at the same time expanding the existing gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:35:16-07:00","id":967526,"title":"","content":"I'll admit to feeling a little disappointed when getting into Requiem 2e that there appeared to be so little new on the horizon, but Rich's answer is just about perfect.<br /> <br /> And for anyone new looking for more Requiem content, don't hesitate to buy the 1e books - every one I've bought has been very easy to translate. Danse Macabre and Damnation City in particular are fantastic and infinitely useful.<br /> <br /> Still, I would buy a 2e Clans &amp; Bloodlines book in an instant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12208-verblet","name":"verblet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:26:39-07:00","id":967621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=966812#post966812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd really rather have Neolithic than Sumerian for werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>*looks at the already existing neolithic werewolf setting*... umm.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-th