nyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:42:37-07:00","id":970174,"title":"","content":"Stew has said he likes the Hunting Grounds features and was planning on putting them in until told to stop. It doesn't seem to be an across-the-line decision for everything in Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:32:58-07:00","id":970234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=970163#post970163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if either of the new books will have additional settings, given that The Pack did and both Signs of Sorcery and The Hedge should, too. Maybe show us what a domain with a long history looks like in Thousand Years of Night; it might be the perfect place to finally do Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div> David has said The Hedge will have an extra setting or two, to help show how the local Freehold shapes the local Hedge.<br /> <br /> Settings in Changeling tend to be more work, partly to reflect the extra mechanics invovled in building them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:58:29-07:00","id":970386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=970165#post970165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Signs won't. Tome of the Pentacle will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you advance us which settings wiil be there? Or is it still too soon?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:24:03-07:00","id":971051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=970155#post970155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they were just including the time line in the title... just to be considerate ya know. <br /> <br /> As a side note a 90s supplement could be cool. Generation X is grown up and doesn't give a shit. Grunge, and alternative rock take the main stage.<br /> MTV starts expanding to more than just music, Bevis and Butthead, reality TV shows. The 80s bubble pops, fraud is at an all time high, and mega corps fold due to fraud. <br /> <br /> Just got new wave requiem and loved it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually now that I think about it. The 90s supplement should be for changling. The forgotten generation... really thematically appropriate. <br /> <br /> So in the spirit of where's the 2e books... changling 2e followed swiftly by a 90s setting supplement please <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:29:43-07:00","id":971265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=966772#post966772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In these three years, the new gamelines (Mummy, Demon) have received much more support than vampire (about 2 or books each one, I think). And I understand perfectly, but I'm concerned. With so much new gamelines, I feel the classical gamelines receve less attention than I'd like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's due to the new gamelines having been kickstarted with lots of supplements as stretch goals. The existing gamelines (VtR, WtF, MtAw, PtC, CtL and HtV) were never planned as Kickstarter campaigns. Thus they don't get as many cool new supplements.<br /> <br /> For Requiem 2.0 I would love to see a (Clans &amp;) Bloodlines book that contains conversions for the most popular bloodlines, and information on how to convert the rest. I don't think the Clanbooks need to be redone at this time, but new material like A Thousand Years of Night would be more than welcome.<br /> <br /> Also, big thanks to Rich Thomas for explaining the delays behind the Requiem 2.0 books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:06:09-07:00","id":973163,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Coveants is in layout. Thousand Years of Night is in Redlines. Half Damned is in First Draft.<br /> <br /> That a good start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:55:24-07:00","id":979995,"title":"","content":"Now that Shattered Dreams is out, how far away you think Secrets of the Covenants is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T16:50:56-07:00","id":980475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=964952#post964952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah it doesn't seem to be that simple at all. I was asking in one of the Monday Meetings if Werewolf was getting a book, as nothing is planned, and RichT responded, 'Not every CofD line will get a book every year between GenCons, we simply don\u2019t have the space to give all 11 lines that many books. But WtF2 will be getting more Dark Eras, and most likely will get more DEs in Dark Eras 2.'<br /> <br /> I don't know what the money situation is at all, maybe World of Darkness does make more and they're trying to get as much as they can before White Wolf takes over, but it doesn't really seem like there's more World of Darkness books, the books they have coming out are leaning towards Vampire because there's only three games out, compared to Chronicle of Darkness' ten, eleven if you count 'blue book, which I do.<br /> <br /> It's frustrating, for those of us who are only really interested in some lines, to not see those lines get support. But, again, I don't know what the business side of things is like beyond what we see from the Monday Meetings, which is admittedly a lot. Some writers can to take a long time with things, because of real life concerns such as 'working to make a living,' and while Mage 20th came out, I think, really fast, Wraith 20 is still being written. Then there's the art direction, which I think only has one full-time worker and someone learning how to do it, dealing with the mercurial and limited pool of artists. It's possible that they just don't have the people to really write and organize and put out more books. There's only so many writers who have the experience and skill to be developers. It's not an easy thing at any level once you get past 'this might be a good idea for a book.'<br /> <br /> And then there's the shift in attention. Vampire doesn't seem as popular as they once were. I see a lot of more on-topic threads in the Vampire forum where someone expresses their moral distaste or disgust in what vampires are and how they don't want to play that, while other games have gotten surprising amounts of attention. And admittedly a lot of the second edition games already have books out from first edition, and a lot of the material can be transferred over, even if it isn't of the quality or with the developmental mindset of second edition. So it makes sense for something like Demon to have several books out, given its popularity, and the fact that some were promised as part of the Kickstarter. And while they may not be out yet, Vampire does have two books coming down the line, and a third planned.<br /> <br /> Even understanding that, the frustration's there. It was like during the Dark Eras voting, where you had one vote out of hundreds, and seeing the lines you like pass by Era-less. I got lucky with Werewolf on the second go around, but Vampire didn't get much beyond Regina, Hunter outside of Salem.<br /> <br /> I think I'd feel at least a little better if I knew how things were going with the whole White Wolf Publishing reincarnation. Will they ever actually do anything? Will they be taking all of World of Darkness properties? If they do, will that mean more steady flow of Chronicles of Darkness books? Or a crunch without the World of Darkness income? Will they be taking writers and artists? There is some overlap.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some of those votes have less to do with Vampire, and more to do with the actual Era that they were competing against. I feel like I could run Vampire in most era's if you give me enough era info. basically they didn't offer me much in the way of Vampire Dark Eras that I was actually interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:08:03-07:00","id":980479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=970386#post970386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you advance us which settings wiil be there? Or is it still too soon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Dave has said in the past that the New York setting, which was too big for the corebook, might appear in Tome of the Pentacle. You may know of it from the fiction in the 2e corebook, which takes place in the New York setting.<br /> <br /> I'd love to have a blogpost about Vampire sometime in the future, maybe with the new co-developer chiming in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T21:12:29-07:00","id":980571,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I also support a vampire blogpost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T03:19:46-07:00","id":981372,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Covenants has moved into proofing. I hope that means it will be available on DriveThru before the end of the month..,.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T09:04:07-07:00","id":981472,"title":"","content":"How long does proofing usually take?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:51:36-07:00","id":981529,"title":"","content":"Indeterminate amount of time. Hopefully a month but sometimes longer. It depends on a lot of things, like how much else is down the pipeline, how big it is. Presumably Secrets of the Covenants is going to have a lot of interesting formatting, which might cause more work fixing little graphical errors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:00:21-07:00","id":982248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=980475#post980475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of those votes have less to do with Vampire, and more to do with the actual Era that they were competing against. I feel like I could run Vampire in most era's if you give me enough era info. basically they didn't offer me much in the way of Vampire Dark Eras that I was actually interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll quote this while echoing several of the other sentiments here: a bit of history reading (ok, a lot) plus some imagination can bridge vampire into various dark eras, especially if VtR 1e and VtM are mined for ideas. With enough research, in fact, you can pretty quickly see how characters (PC and NPC alike) could roll forward into a cascade of events that would keep them busy for a long, long time to come.<br /> <br /> That's where Thousand Years of Night comes in--or at least I hope it does, in presenting the broad strokes of kindred existence as well as why elders are scary beyond just their ability to put so many plays in the game at once. <br /> <br /> TYoN is, as I understand it, a product that will color in an area for vampires that is--purposefully in fact--left vague by the main focus on modern nights. To me at least the stretch of history and the impact of said history on people (kindred) as everything about humanity collides over time is the most interesting part of vampire as a game idea. Timelining characters through such chop is my idea of fun, twisted though that might be.<br /> <br /> So, bring on those thousand years!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:58:46-07:00","id":985825,"title":"","content":"I wonder if half damned will cover what happens if a vampire tries to breed with something other then a mortal to create a Dampyr, like an Oneiron (which produce Cambions when they breed with mortals), when vampires breed with Werewolves, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T18:03:41-07:00","id":985827,"title":"","content":"Can't wait for Secret of the Covenants. I love the idea of smashing together splats into one big hardcover. Give me that and Secret to the Clans and I'll essentially have everything I need for VtR (not that it's everything I'll buy. A Thousand Years of Night sounds very <i>very </i>enticing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T20:30:00-07:00","id":985913,"title":"","content":"Oh man, if there was a Secrets of the Clans in the works that would be amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T20:42:37-07:00","id":985921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=985913#post985913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man, if there was a Secrets of the Clans in the works that would be amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They've got to be planning for that, right?<br /> <br /> <i><b>RIGHT!?</b></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T01:35:22-07:00","id":987150,"title":"","content":"I highly doubt that it's a priority for them, given that Clanbooks are still quite relevant and not as outdated as most other 1e material","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T09:12:50-07:00","id":987291,"title":"","content":"Most of the mechanical elements from the Clan books made it into 2e in some form or another, and all of the fiction (which was 90% of the books) is still applicable. I don't see much need for a Secrets of the Clans. For the elements that didn't make it into 2e like Malkavia, Hollow Mekhet, and the Red Surrender, I'm sure they'll eventually find their way into 2e in various supplement books. Meanwhile there's no shortage of homebrew for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:56:27-07:00","id":987458,"title":"","content":"Oh I know, but I can dream. By the way, what are the Hollow Mekhet and Red Surrender? I'm a little unfamiliar with those terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T15:57:45-07:00","id":987475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=987458#post987458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I know, but I can dream. By the way, what are the Hollow Mekhet and Red Surrender? I'm a little unfamiliar with those terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hollow Mekhet are a weird branch of the clan that date back to Ancient Egypt, where the Embrace is performed upon a corpse and they become Kindred hunted by their reflection/shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:07:10-07:00","id":987482,"title":"","content":"The Red Surrender is letting your Beast sort of take over. Not for a fight, like in a frenzy, but for other things. It can be addicting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:04:24-07:00","id":987838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=987291#post987291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the mechanical elements from the Clan books made it into 2e in some form or another, and all of the fiction (which was 90% of the books) is still applicable. I don't see much need for a Secrets of the Clans. For the elements that didn't make it into 2e like Malkavia, Hollow Mekhet, and the Red Surrender, I'm sure they'll eventually find their way into 2e in various supplement books. Meanwhile there's no shortage of homebrew for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's fair! I've been meaning to dig into the clan books.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There's just a certain compulsive part of me that loves the idea of a core book, a covenant fatsplat, and a clan fatsplat (and seeing that model applied to the different lines). I think ChroD is unique from WoD in that each line can sustain a pretty modest book count that covers pretty much everything you could want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:30:45-07:00","id":987852,"title":"","content":"2e Vampire basically (and I feel in some way more than any other line) just needs the big old 1e Patch book. Actually in some ways the 2e book is this... which is why in some ways I feel it still needs more work. IIRC Rose? said that she would have done some stuff differently if she had know that B&amp;S was 2e.<br /> <br /> So I wouldn't mind a Clan book even if the major reason was just to provide those updated mechanics and perhaps a summarized retread of the clan books ('cause I'm probably not going to go buy books with outdated mechanics). Heck, I wouldn't complain if they wanted to republish them with updated mechanics, that might get me to buy them.<br /> <br /> Also we need a book on just the Strix, &quot;The Parliament of Owls&quot;. For potential inspiration, we were talking about Neolithic Era on the slack channel and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1923_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1923\" data-vbnamecard=\"1923\">BigDamnHero</a> said he was going to do Owl as a Pangaean, and I suggested he make Owl the Strix progenitor. All kinds of fun places you can go, what if owl splits to become the Strix to survive? what if the Strix were already its children but to survive/punish humanity for its trangression it binds itself into the first vampires? etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:48:13-07:00","id":987864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=987852#post987852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e Vampire basically (and I feel in some way more than any other line) just needs the big old 1e Patch book. Actually in some ways the 2e book is this... which is why in some ways I feel it still needs more work. IIRC Rose? said that she would have done some stuff differently if she had know that B&amp;S was 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>She did say that, though it was more in reference to the way it was laid out than to the mechanics. The thing is, when 2e was still being billed as &quot;Chronicle books with optional rules updates,&quot; they were making layout decisions based on the assumption that a given Chronicle book might be the only 2e book the group owned. That's why they're more-or-less standalone instead of using 1e's core rules in one book and gameline-specific rules in splat books model, for example. That's also why Requiem leaves it up to inference that vampires don't gain Willpower from sleep instead of calling it out specifically. Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle was designed to be a complete rulebook for playing vampires under what was called The World of Darkness Rules Revision, so if the complete vampire book doesn't say characters regain Willpower from sleeping, they don't.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm pretty sure both Werewolf and Mage were already in at least second drafts by the time the decision was made to call Second Edition what it was, so this isn't exactly a phenomenon unique to Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:12:50-07:00","id":988585,"title":"","content":"I have essentially forgotten that Vampire 2E exists. I own the core book, but I haven't looked at it for a long while, because it's just sort of there. There are other, more interesting books drawing my attention. This is what happens when you don't put out material that grabs a customer's attention and inspires him to give a crap. I'm running a Mage 2E chronicle and I'm really excited about Changeling 2E. I already have plans for a Changeling chronicle that's going to pick up right where my Mage chronicle leaves things off.<br /> <br /> Giving a little bit of attention to the game line in something like Dark Eras was nice. It's a big book, though, and it has more interesting stuff in it. Stuff that feels more relevant.<br /> <br /> There are so many more interesting game lines out there. So much more interesting material being, you know, published. And I'm not loyal to any one game line. I have run my fair share of Vampire 1E chronicles. Own all the books. And while I know that there's still plenty of material there, but it's not drawing my attention, because OPP keeps publishing new stuff. This new stuff feels more interesting simply because it's new. I know that's a little shallow, but it's also basic human psychology.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll get back to Vampire 2E in another 2-3 years. Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","user":"TelperionST","date":". 10-16-2016, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:19:28-07:00","id":988590,"title":"","content":"They can only produce as many books as they can produce in as much time as they can produce them. I'm not gonna pretend it doesn't suck that they haven't been able to put anything new out for Requiem in so long but it is what it is. There's not really much that can be done about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:00:18-07:00","id":988632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=988590#post988590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can only produce as many books as they can produce in as much time as they can produce them. I'm not gonna pretend it doesn't suck that they haven't been able to put anything new out for Requiem in so long but it is what it is. There's not really much that can be done about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a cop out. Creating an ever increasing amount of game lines is a conscious decision. Every company in the world has a limited amount of resources, so most of the existing ones concentrate on what works. Look, I don't agree with, or even like, all of the business decisions that OPP seems to be making. As an individual customer my opinion is largely meaningless. However, from a customer retention standpoint these decisions do matter. At the same time I realize that this is as much a passion project turned into a business as anything else. So, ultimately, talking about the topic is pointless. No one is going to listen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:21:13-07:00","id":988648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=988632#post988632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's a cop out. Creating an ever increasing amount of game lines is a conscious decision. Every company in the world has a limited amount of resources, so most of the existing ones concentrate on what works. Look, I don't agree with, or even like, all of the business decisions that OPP seems to be making. As an individual customer my opinion is largely meaningless. However, from a customer retention standpoint these decisions do matter. At the same time I realize that this is as much a passion project turned into a business as anything else. So, ultimately, talking about the topic is pointless. No one is going to listen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Four people work for this company as permanent employees and there's only so many hours in a day. I'd rather scarcer books come out and be good than be on the treadmill of mediocre shit that, say D&amp;D or even old White Wolf fell into so often back in the 90s and 2000s. While I'd absolutely love to have Thousand Years of Night in my hands tomorrow and four more books on the docket, the fact remains that tabletop RPGs are scarcely a profitable industry and we're not feasibly going to get a stream of new content without market forces drastically changing or the freelancers all being disgustingly underpaid. Why do you think OPP does so many Kickstarters? It's a way of guaranteeing buyer interest without sinking months of labor into a product only to see it barely sell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:55:52-07:00","id":988666,"title":"","content":"One thing I perceived as a sort of problem with production has already been fixed, with three or four new freelancers being trained to help with the second part of development. I imagine it's been a long time in the making, I recall mentions of Mirthful Mike Chaney training someone a while ago.<br /> <br /> But your problem is, you admitted, 'New things catch my interest.' Even if vampire put out things, so are other lines and you would still be interested in them. With that mindset, once vampire puts out stuff your interest will be rekindled. Either way, you are still purchasing products that allow for vampire, and other lines, to get work done.<br /> <br /> All that said, while I appreciate you say you're not interested in vampire right now you still have the book and can still play it at any time, such as when new material comes out. Or you may never. I've never played Werewolf the Apocalypse but I still have the book. Buying new products you're interested in lets the company know you're interested in them, and gives them money to make new books, hire new people, and put out more stuff we can all enjoy.<br /> <br /> Honestly this has already been responded to by Rich Thomas in an earlier post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T02:45:09-07:00","id":988752,"title":"","content":"I mean, it's not like we haven't seen <i>any</i> new material since 2E dropped. Just none in book form that we can give Onyx Path money for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T03:50:49-07:00","id":988773,"title":"","content":"I think the most important fact we can take from this thread are its 3557 views and 75 answers. People is paying attention to the subject &quot;When will we have the next Requiem book&quot;. So... pretty please, hurry up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:39:18-07:00","id":989069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=988590#post988590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can only produce as many books as they can produce in as much time as they can produce them. I'm not gonna pretend it doesn't suck that they haven't been able to put anything new out for Requiem in so long but it is what it is. There's not really much that can be done about it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Can't say I agree with you, since obviously they can produce X amount of content, seems more like they simply didn't allocate resources to do so? perhaps they shouldn't release 4 core books in one year? and 3 books in one line in one year (I think a bunch of Demon books happened in ~1 year)? maybe if resources had been allocated differently... As excited as I've been for Werewolf, Beast, Mage, and Promethean, and as much as I loved all of the Demon books, I'm sad that Demon won't get more supplements (outside of Dark Eras) for a while, and I've felt a bit overwhelmed with new core books. Maybe it's good 'cause it'll mean that everything will be 2e sooner than later. I can't help but thing though that Werewolf's first supplement could have waited a bit longer? It's hard to say whether I think the push should be to get all lines on 2e, instead of focusing on supplements... if that's the goal then I think it should be communicated. If not, then it would seem that it would be possible given the number of books pushed to have a supplement for each at least every other year, if you don't try to push as many core books at once. It'd probably almost be possible to have a supplement for each book each year if handled right","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:53:49-07:00","id":989076,"title":"","content":"I can understand them wanting to get 2e core books out, and I don't begrudge them that. I do hope we see a decent number of Requiem supplements over the next year or two, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:59:07-07:00","id":989077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=989069#post989069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Can't say I agree with you, since obviously they can produce X amount of content, seems more like they simply didn't allocate resources to do so? perhaps they shouldn't release 4 core books in one year? and 3 books in one line in one year (I think a bunch of Demon books happened in ~1 year)? maybe if resources had been allocated differently... As excited as I've been for Werewolf, Beast, Mage, and Promethean, and as much as I loved all of the Demon books, I'm sad that Demon won't get more supplements (outside of Dark Eras) for a while, and I've felt a bit overwhelmed with new core books. Maybe it's good 'cause it'll mean that everything will be 2e sooner than later. I can't help but thing though that Werewolf's first supplement could have waited a bit longer? It's hard to say whether I think the push should be to get all lines on 2e, instead of focusing on supplements... if that's the goal then I think it should be communicated. If not, then it would seem that it would be possible given the number of books pushed to have a supplement for each at least every other year, if you don't try to push as many core books at once. It'd probably almost be possible to have a supplement for each book each year if handled right</div> </div> </div> </div>I think getting everything up to speed with 2e is pretty clearly the priority. Demon got a lot of supplements right away because Kickstarter. I'm assuming the same will happen with Beast and Deviant. All of the upcoming vampire supplements were on the schedule before The Pack, but Rose had personal complications get in the way and Stu did not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T17:17:19-07:00","id":989081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=989077#post989077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think getting everything up to speed with 2e is pretty clearly the priority. Demon got a lot of supplements right away because Kickstarter. I'm assuming the same will happen with Beast and Deviant. All of the upcoming vampire supplements were on the schedule before The Pack, but Rose had personal complications get in the way and Stu did not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I heard that Rose had some stuff going on at the time. I wasn't sure if she was doing better or not, but I hope she is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T20:21:49-07:00","id":989172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=989077#post989077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think getting everything up to speed with 2e is pretty clearly the priority. Demon got a lot of supplements right away because Kickstarter. I'm assuming the same will happen with Beast and Deviant. All of the upcoming vampire supplements were on the schedule before The Pack, but Rose had personal complications get in the way and Stu did not.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, just not sure that I like the &quot;all the supplements at once&quot; approach, seems like it would be better to spread them out.<br /> <br /> That said, I am of course aware there were some extenuating circumstances with a few of these things. I read rich's post, and am aware that Matt and Dave? also had life things last year.<br /> <br /> It just seems to me, that if they weren't doing all supplements at once, interest would maintain over time with a supplement per year, those supplements would be able to answer more of the questions we have because we'd have more time to play and ask. The people who do the work could spread broader. I'm making some assumptions of course that that's feasible, and given some other knowledge perhaps it would not have been possible to have Demon dev's working on Vampire, instead of cranking out Demon supplements (that said I love them all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:30:25-07:00","id":989186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/964724-whens-next-2nd-edition-book-coming-out?p=989172#post989172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah, just not sure that I like the &quot;all the supplements at once&quot; approach, seems like it would be better to spread them out.<br /> <br /> That said, I am of course aware there were some extenuating circumstances with a few of these things. I read rich's post, and am aware that Matt and Dave? also had life things last year.<br /> <br /> It just seems to me, that if they weren't doing all supplements at once, interest would maintain over time with a supplement per year, those supplements would be able to answer more of the questions we have because we'd have more time to play and ask. The people who do the work could spread broader. I'm making some assumptions of course that that's feasible, and given some other knowledge perhaps it would not have been possible to have Demon dev's working on Vampire, instead of cranking out Demon supplements (that said I love them all).</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Demon supplements got made at the rate they did because Kickstarter backers already expressed interest in them and helped pay for their existence preemptively; that makes a lot more sense from a business standpoint than &quot;well, someone really wants to make this Werewolf supplement, lets spend a year getting writers and artists together and slap it all together in the hopes that it'll sell enough copies in DriveThru to cover production costs.&quot; Crowdfunding is literally the only sure money in a largely unprofitable industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakk